0,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"The music of Australia has an extensive history made of music societies. Indigenous Australian music forms a significant part of the unique heritage of a 40,000- to 60,000-year history which produced the iconic didgeridoo. Contemporary fusions of indigenous and Western styles are exemplified in the works of Yothu Yindi, No Fixed Address, Geoffrey Gurrumul Yunupingu and Christine Anu, and mark ...",Wik-Epa,Australian
1,Australian music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/?title=Australian_music&redirect=no,"Appearance Redirect page Redirect to: Music of Australia Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License 4.0 Terms of Use Privacy Policy Wikimedia Foundation, Inc.",Wik-Epa,Australian
2,The Record: Australian Music On Wikipedia - Wikimedia Australia,https://wikimedia.org.au/wiki/The_Record:_Australian_Music_On_Wikipedia,"Through four edit-a-thon events across Australia, The Record will grow the low number of Wikipedia articles about Australian musicians, organisations and publications. Volunteers will be invited to be trained to edit, expand, and create new articles related to a diverse range of Australian music and musicians.",Wik-Epa,Australian
3,Music of Australia - The Art and Popular Culture Encyclopedia,https://www.artandpopularculture.com/Australian_music,"The music of Australia has an extensive history made of music societies. Indigenous Australian music is a part of the unique heritage of a 40,000-60,000 year history which produced the iconic didgeridoo.",Wik-Epa,Australian
4,1 - Introduction and Historiography of Music in Australia,https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/cambridge-companion-to-music-in-australia/introduction-and-historiography-of-music-in-australia/0AA9EED9FB4A3033FA98A4B1435981CC,"This Introduction provides an account of how Music in Australia has been conceptualised in previous music histories. It shows that music historians have sought to draw boundaries around what Australian music is by emphasizing the milestones of European settlement, and have often struggled to reconcile Indigenous music making and non-Indigenous music into one account of music in Australia. It ...",Wik-Epa,Australian
5,A history of Australian music in 6 objects - Double J,https://www.abc.net.au/listen/doublej/music-reads/lists/a-history-of-australian-music-in-6-objects/10343512,"Australian music has a new home. The Australian Music Vault is now open in Melbourne, nestled among the Arts Centre Melbourne, Hamer Hall, and the National Gallery of Victoria in the city's ...",Wik-Epa,Australian
6,Sounds of the Land Down Under: A Journey Through Australian Music - CIEE,https://www.ciee.org/go-abroad/college-study-abroad/blog/sounds-land-down-under-journey-through-australian-music,"From iconic bands and legendary artists to emerging talent, Australian music has left an indelible mark on the global stage. Join us as we embark on a musical journey through the sounds of the land down under, exploring the rich tapestry of Australian music and the artists who have shaped its unique identity.",Wik-Epa,Australian
7,12 Iconic Australian Songs You Should Know - Culture Trip,https://theculturetrip.com/pacific/australia/articles/12-iconic-australian-songs-you-should-know,"The patriotic song of Down Under has become an iconic Australian song across the world, topping the music charts in the 1980s in many countries, including Australia, Britain and the US.",Wik-Epa,Australian
